"""The synthetic corpus for the signal-first goldens (test plan T0.1).

``python tests/fixtures/signal_first/build_corpus.py`` writes ``corpus/`` next to this file. The
generated bytes are COMMITTED, so a golden compares against fixed input rather than against
whatever this script produces on the day. ``tests/regression/test_signal_first_corpus.py`` proves
the two agree.

Deliberately independent of the code under test: it imports neither ``RECORD_COLUMNS`` nor
``MASTER_COLS``, and writes every column name literally, so a change to those constants cannot
quietly rewrite a golden's input. The only repo import is ``gtm_core.fictionalize``, which turns
placeholder seeds (never a real name) into obviously fictional identities.

Layout written under ``corpus/``::

    profiles/sigfirst/...            the fictional tenant's knowledge
    state/sigfirst/...               its state (seeded as content/; the repo ignores a dir named
                                     content/): exports, pool, ledger, captures, sequences
    lists/gen1.csv gen2.csv gen3.csv the three historical pool layouts, one list each
"""

